# Pod-C for a single-socket worker: ONE Guaranteed neighbor Pod, 24 exclusive cores.
# Same per-socket pressure as pod-c (saturates the LLC and the memory
# controllers), but with a single Pod because there is no second socket.
#
# 24 cores is 48 CPUs with SMT on, so on a 36-core socket this leaves room for
# only a few pinned streams; check the planner's "at most N streams" error.
#
# One Pod means the socket-split check does not apply, so
# NOISY_NEIGHBOR_REQUIRE_SOCKET_SPLIT is left unset. Do not use this profile on a
# two-socket worker: it would leave one socket quiet.
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_ARGS="--stream 24
--stream-index 0
--stream-l3-size 512M
--metrics-brief
--timeout 0
--log-file stress-ng.log"
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_SCOPE=pod
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_CPU_REQUEST=24
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_MEMORY_REQUEST=16Gi
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_MEMORY_LIMIT=16Gi
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_POD_COUNT=1
NOISY_NEIGHBOR_GUARANTEED=1
